@startuml
left to right direction

title Use Case Diagram for AI-Powered Analysis & Insights System

rectangle "System" {
  usecase "CFR001: View Financial Insights Dashboard" as CFR001
  usecase "SAFR002: Manage Fraud Alerts" as SAFR002
  usecase "CFR003: View Predictive Analytics" as CFR003
  usecase "CFR004: Receive Personalized Recommendations" as CFR004
  usecase "CFR005: Adjust Recommendation Preferences" as CFR005
  usecase "CFR006: Monitor Spending Limits" as CFR006
  usecase "CFR007: Discover Investment Opportunities" as CFR007
  usecase "CFR008: Stay Informed with News" as CFR008
  usecase "CFR009: Access Consolidated Dashboard" as CFR010
  usecase "CFR010: Manage Data Sharing with Advisors" as CFR010

  usecase "SAFR003: Adjust Analysis Parameters for Clients" as SAFR003
  usecase "FAFR002: View Client Intervention Alerts" as FAFR002
  usecase "FAFR004: Configure Segmented Analysis" as FAFR004

  usecase "SFR019: Maintain Historical Record of Insights" as SFR019
  usecase "AIFR003: Detect Unusual Spending Patterns" as AIFR003
  usecase "AIFR005: Identify Investment Opportunities" as AIFR005

  Client --> CFR001 : View financial data in a dashboard.
  SysAdmin -> SAFR002 : Manage fraud alerts settings for the system.
  
  // Financial Advisor to FAFR
  FAFR004 <|-- (FAFR) : Configure analysis parameters based on client segments.

  Client --> CFR003 : View predictive financial trends and market insights.
  Client -> AIFR001: Request predictions from AI for future financial scenarios.
  
  Client -> SFR002: Receive personalized recommendations aligned with their profile.
  SysAdmin --+> SAFR004 : Adjust system-wide analysis parameters.

  // System to other use cases
  Sys --> CFR005 : Allow clients to adjust personalization settings via the system.
  Sys --> AIFR006: Generate spending limit alerts when thresholds are exceeded by users.
  
  Client --+> SFR019 : Historical data is managed for trend analysis.

  // Financial Advisor interactions
  FAFR002 <|-- (FAFR) : View client-specific intervention alerts generated via the system.
  Sys --> AIFR008: Generate predictive interventions based on user financial behavior patterns.
  
  Client -> CFR010 : Manage data sharing permissions with advisors through the system.

  // AI System use cases
  AIFR007 <|-- (AIFR) : Extract relevant news for portfolios from the system's knowledge base.
}

@enduml